-- title:
--   Fixed field of the level automorphisms for q = 3
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime equal to $3$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $\zeta$ be an element of `Idx q`, that is, a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Write $F =$ `fieldBar q M'` for the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((Q))$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ obtained by adjoining to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ the coefficientwise images of the function field `xHFunctionField` of level $q^2M'$ attached to the subgroup `levelH q M'`, the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$. For each $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$, `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` is the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra automorphism of $F$ satisfying the predicate `IsLevelAutBar q M' ζ γ` when such an automorphism exists, and the identity otherwise; `IsLevelAutBar` requires that, for every weight $k$, every pair of modular forms $f,g$ of weight $k$ on $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$ and $p_g$ having nonzero image, and every ring embedding $\iota : \overline{\mathbb Q} \to \mathbb C$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$, the $\iota$-image of the value of the automorphism on the ratio of the series of $p_f$ and $p_g$ times the $q$-expansion of $g \mid_k \gamma^{\sharp}$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f \mid_k \gamma^{\sharp}$, where $\gamma^\sharp$ is `conjElem q γ`. Assume $x \in F$ is fixed by `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$. The conclusion is that there exists a Laurent series $g$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying in the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise images of `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (Gamma0 M')` (the field generated over $\mathbb Q$ by ratios of series of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of equal weight on $\Gamma_0(M')$) such that $x$, viewed as a Laurent series, equals `qExpand` of $g$, i.e. the series obtained from $g$ by multiplying every exponent by $q$.
--
--   This identifies the fixed field of the level automorphisms indexed by $\Gamma_0(M')$ acting on the full-level function field as the set of level-$\Gamma_0(M')$ functions of $Q^q$, equivalently $g(qz)$; it is the $q = 3$ case, the hypothesis $q = 3$ replacing the condition $q \ge 5$ used in the companion statement. The argument combines the finiteness of the group generated by the level automorphisms, the lower bound $q(q^2-1) \le 2\,|G|$, and the upper bound on the relative degree of the subfield generated by the image of `qExpand`; it is used in the identification of the relevant ring of integral $q$-expansions at level $q = 3$.
